# Firdoch Core is every creature type in every zone (CR 702.73a, 604.3): in the library it is an Insect card, so Grist's
# +1 ("If an Insect card was milled this way, put a loyalty counter on Grist and repeat this process") repeats when the
# Core is milled, though the Core is no creature card (a Kindred Artifact). Llanowar Elves, milled next, is a Creature
# - Elf Druid and not an Insect (the control): the process ends there. Two passes: two tokens, two cards milled, and one
# loyalty counter for the Core on top of the +1 itself (3 + 1 + 1 = 5).

[Bot1 Deck]
Bayou x3
Grist, the Hunger Tide
Forest x5
Firdoch Core
Llanowar Elves
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Bayou.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bayou.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bayou.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Bayou#1.Activate(Ability: Add {B})
Bot1.Battlefield.Bayou#2.Activate(Ability: Add {G})
Bot1.Battlefield.Bayou#3.Activate(Ability: Add {G})
Bot1.Hand.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Activate(Ability: +1)
[T5 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Grist, the Hunger Tide.Counters.Loyalty = 5
Bot1.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Firdoch Core
